Z||000003||cmyokley||10-22-1999||05:39 PM||||Ayamnik,<P>I would like to know more about your 4.3L install, how is it going, what problems have you had etc... I have not seen any info on the 4.3 swap, are there threads on this forum I have missed? Do you have any pics yet? Please lead me to more info on this swap, I just can't believe that it would be the best answer, a high HP v6 vs: the weight problems with a V8 swap.<P>Any answers would help me get started.<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000004||batboy||10-22-1999||08:06 PM||||Yes, we've had a couple different discussions about the 4.3 swap. Not many people have done it yet, but in my opinion, it should be a great swap. The 4.3 is a powerful, torquey, and reliable engine. Lots of hipo parts available. You have to use a V8 adapter plate and a custom flywheel in most cases. Squid (one of the Forum members) seems quite knowledgeable about this swap. He has most of the parts rounded up and is going to do this project in the near future.||||reg||1
Z||000005||jhogans||10-22-1999||09:10 PM||||Where does a 4.3 engine come from?  What kinds of performance can one expect from such a swap? (ie HP, torque, etc.)||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||10-22-1999||10:15 PM||||GM used the 4.3 in lots of S-10 trucks, full size trucks and Astro minivans. With a performance roller cam, headers, etc. a 4.3 should easily make 250 HP and 300 ft/lbs of torque.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Greg Piet||10-23-1999||02:33 AM||||When I hear the idea of a 4.3 in a fiero, I just druel thinking about a 4.3litre twin turbo cyclone/typhoon motor.  I remember those corvette killer trucks, and with that in a fiero, it just sounds lethal.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mwbackus||10-23-1999||07:48 AM||||Actually, the Syclones/Typhoon turbo 4.3 uses a single turbo design.  I have already purchased one (expensive!) for my winter project.  I plan on a rebuild and then install into an 88 coupe (when I find one cheap enough).  There are many areas of the 4.3 turbo engine that are in need of improvement to provide a good dependable powerplant, longevity has been an issue on the stock motors in the past.  The intercooler system is also a challenge in the limited confines of the Fiero engine compartment.  This is not an "easy" swap, since the whole accessory drive belt system requires a redesign.  I have found some very good info on the 4.3 Turbo motor here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.syty.org/syty.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.syty.org/syty.html</A> <P>Nice bunch of guys on their mailing list, their helpful attitudes remind me very much of our own little forum.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||10-23-1999||09:17 AM||||Racing 4.3 engines have won all sorts of championships. Here is a pic of one awesome modified 4.3L, sure wish it was mine, but it's not. With those expensive aluminum splayed-valve heads, the power output is better than a lot of small block V8's.<P> <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/43motor.jpg"> ||||reg||1
